{"name":"Observatory","hex":"#008f70","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"observatory","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where stars, planets and other celestial bodies are observed, usually through a telescope; also place for observing meteorological or other natural phenomena.","A lookout (vantage point with a view of the surrounding area)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/observatory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Observatory","blocks":[{"text":"An observatory is a location used for observing terrestrial, marine, or celestial events. Astronomy, climatology/meteorology, geophysics, oceanography and volcanology are examples of disciplines for which observatories have been constructed. Some people still prefer to restrict the term to astronomical observatories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Royal_observatory_Greenwich.JPG/330px-Royal_observatory_Greenwich.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Observatory","wikidata":"Q62832"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/ALMA%E2%80%99s_Solitude01.jpg/500px-ALMA%E2%80%99s_Solitude01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/ALMA%E2%80%99s_Solitude01.jpg/1280px-ALMA%E2%80%99s_Solitude01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/ALMA%E2%80%99s_Solitude01.jpg/500px-ALMA%E2%80%99s_Solitude01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AALMA%E2%80%99s_Solitude01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/20041225-Paranal.jpg/500px-20041225-Paranal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https